NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5002
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-supabase-anon-key

# ── The onboarding / portal API (mbp-backend) ────────────────────────────────
#
# Read at build time, so a change needs a dev-server restart or a rebuild.
#
# There is no fixture or mock mode any more: every page — gym wizard, gym portal, gym login,
# admin — talks to whichever stage this points at. Set it to the sandbox to walk a flow.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MBP_API_URL points at a stage. Unset means https://api.muscleboxpro.com, and
# that default is load-bearing in three places at once: it is the origin allowed in
# connect-src, it is the host that makes the session cookies same-site, and it is the host
# on which the sandbox bearer hatch refuses to operate. Setting it to an execute-api URL
# turns all three on together, deliberately — see rule 4 in client/src/lib/apiClient.ts.
#
# Note the stage is part of the path: .../sandbox, with no trailing slash. Dropping the
# stage answers 403 "Missing Authentication Token", which does not look like the mistake
# it is.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MBP_API_URL=https://6t9q5v5v97.execute-api.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/sandbox

# ── The two franchise APIs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Required in sandbox, and only in sandbox. The franchise routes did not fit in the onboarding
# stack (484 of CloudFormation's 500 resources), so they live in MbpFranchiseAdmin and
# MbpFranchiseWizard. On api.muscleboxpro.com those are two base paths on one host and
# apiClient derives both, so neither variable is needed. In sandbox they are two unrelated
# execute-api hostnames, which cannot be derived from anything — apiClient resolves them to
# null and every franchise call fails with a console error naming the variable to set, rather
# than sending a franchise request to the onboarding host and getting a 403 that reads like an
# undeployed route.
#
# Both values are the stack's ApiUrl output, stage included, no trailing slash. The base
# path (/franchise-admin, /franchise-wizard) is *not* part of them: it only exists on the custom
# domain. NEXT_PUBLIC_MBP_FRANCHISE_API_URL serves /admin/franchises*, so the admin panel's
# franchise tab is blank without it even though the rest of /admin works.
#
#   aws cloudformation describe-stacks --stack-name MbpFranchiseAdmin-sandbox \
#     --query "Stacks[0].Outputs[?OutputKey=='ApiUrl'].OutputValue" --output text
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MBP_FRANCHISE_API_URL=https://76d9t56zx1.execute-api.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/sandbox
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MBP_FRANCHISE_WIZARD_API_URL=https://<id>.execute-api.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/sandbox

# ── The franchise documents bucket ───────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Required wherever the wizard's step 3 is used, **production included**, which is what makes this
# unlike the three above. A franchisee's PAN or Aadhaar scan is PUT straight to S3 from the browser
# with a presigned URL, so the bytes never pass through a Lambda and there is no version of the
# upload that goes through api.muscleboxpro.com. The CSP therefore has to name the bucket, and
# next.config.mjs will only accept an mbp-franchise-docs-*.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com origin over
# https. Anything else is ignored rather than allowed.
#
# Origin only: no key, no path, no trailing slash. The bucket is mbp-franchise-docs-<env>-<account>,
# so it cannot be derived from anything the frontend knows.
#
# Without it the presign succeeds, the PUT is blocked by the browser, and the console says CSP while
# the screen says the upload failed.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MBP_FRANCHISE_DOCS_ORIGIN=https://mbp-franchise-docs-sandbox-<account>.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com
